# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Driver app → backend API URL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# By default the app AUTO-DETECTS your computer's LAN IP from the Metro dev host,
# so it follows your Wi-Fi / IP automatically and you normally DON'T need to set
# anything here.
#
# To force a specific address, UNCOMMENT one of the lines below (remove the "#")
# and restart Expo with:  npx expo start -c
#
# • Manual LAN IP (find yours with:  ipconfig getifaddr en0):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.243.71.14:8000/api/v1
#
# • Android emulator (host machine):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000/api/v1
#
# • Deployed backend:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.your-domain.com/api/v1
